# No union switch in JSX

JSX **composes** a value. It does not discriminate a domain union or
assemble English. `"key" in x ? … : "other" in x ? …` inside markup is a
type probe dressed as UI. `{" "}` glued onto a ternary is the same bug.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — union sniff + sentence built in the banner
<ConfirmBanner>
  {"item" in pending.item ? (
    <>Item <strong>{itemName(ctx, pending.item.item)}</strong></>
  ) : "section" in pending.item ? (
    <>Section <strong>{pending.item.section.title}</strong></>
  ) : null}{" "}
  will be removed.
</ConfirmBanner>

// ✅ GOOD — named formatter owns the union; JSX is one child
<ConfirmBanner>{pendingRemoveCopy(pending.item, name)}</ConfirmBanner>
```

Put the `in` / discriminant in **one named function** that returns the
finished `ReactNode` (or string). Import that helper — do not paste the
ladder into a second demo (`unify-demo-chrome.mdc`).

If the call site already has the concrete variant (the click that queued
remove), format there and pass the message. Do not make the banner reverse
the union.

Related: `names-establish-meaning.mdc`, `unify-demo-chrome.mdc`,
`demos-are-wiring.mdc`.
